=== QT008 QT009 QT013 | juxtaposed with a string, which the masked view cannot see
a1:til "3"
a2:where "ab"
a3:flip "ab"

=== QT012 QT008 | a one-char string is an atom, and a symbol vector is not a count
a4:distinct "a"
a5:til `a`b

=== clean | the string shapes q accepts
b1:sum "ab"
b2:distinct "ab"
b3:where ""
b4:til `a
b5:til 0x01
b6:ratios "ab"

=== clean | a builtin name inside a string followed by a string is not a call
s:("x til ";"3")

=== QT014 | the infix form, which is how rotate is written
r:3.5 rotate 1 2

=== QT017 | a char is no window size, infix too
r:"a" mavg 1 2 3

=== QT019 | within with a three-item right operand
r:x within 1 2 3

=== QT018 | cor of two literal vectors of different lengths
r:1 2 cor 1 2 3

=== QT014 | a name before the literal does not change which operand it is
r:f 1.5 rotate 1 2

=== QT014 | nor does a statement before it on the line
r:2 mavg 1 2 3;r2:3.5 rotate 1 2

=== clean | the infix forms q accepts
r1:1 rotate 1 2
r2:2 mavg 1 2 3
r3:x within 1 2
r4:1 2 cor 1 2
r5:1 rotate 1 2,3

=== clean | an infix right operand that runs on is not the literal
r:x within 1 2 3,4


=== clean | an int vector counts (q 5: where 1 2i is 0 1 1)
r:where 1 2i

=== QT009 | a short one does not (q 5: where 1 2h is 'type)
r:where 1 2h

=== QT009 | nor does an atom (q 5: where 2 is 'type)
r:where 2

=== QT009 | a boolean atom either (q 5: where 1b is 'type)
r:where 1b

=== clean profile: general | the where phrase of a query takes a boolean atom (q 5 runs each, #737)
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
empty:select from t where 0b
all1:exec a from t where 1b
f:{[t] delete from t where 0b}

=== QT009 profile: general | before from, where is still the function (q 5: select v:where 1b from t is 'type)
t:([]a:1 2)
r:select v:where 1b from t

=== QT009 | a byte vector with something in it (q 5: where 0x01 and where 0x0102 are 'type)
r:where 0x01
s:where 0x0102

=== clean | the empty byte vector holds nothing to refuse (q 5: where 0x is `long$())
r:where 0x

=== clean | an enlisted atom is a list (q 5: where enlist 2 is 0 0)
r:where enlist 2

=== QD001 | til of a null or negative infinity (q 5: til 0N and til -0W are 'domain)
a:til 0N
b:til -0W

=== QD001 | and of infinity (q 5: til 0W and til 0Wj are 'limit)
c:til 0W
d:til 0Wj

=== clean | a short infinity is only a count (q 5: count til 0Wh is 32767)
e:til 0Wh

=== QT013 | flip of a symbol, even one naming a table (q 5: flip `t is 'rank)
d:flip `a

=== QA010 | the dyadic keywords refuse a third argument (q 5: xasc[`a;t;1] and bin[1 2 3;2;1] are 'rank)
a:xasc[`a;t;1]
b:bin[1 2 3;2;1]

=== QA010 | ssr takes three, wj four, md5 one (q 5: 'rank past each)
c:ssr["a";"b";"c";1]
d:wj[a;b;c;d;e]
e:md5["a";"b"]

=== clean | the arity each takes
a:xasc[`a;t]
